Design a test for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: newNode
Signature: struct node* newNode(int item)
Description: /**
 * @brief Allocate and initialize a new binary tree node.
 *
 * Creates a new node with the specified key and sets its left and right
 * child pointers to NULL. The function allocates memory for the node and
 * does not initialize any other fields.
 *
 * @param item Value to assign to the node's key field.
 *
 * @return Pointer to the newly allocated node on success, or NULL if
 *         memory allocation fails.
 *
 * @note Memory: Caller is responsible for freeing the returned node.
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called newNode
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

struct node {
	int key;
	struct node *left, *right;
};

// Target function implementation
struct node* newNode(int item)
{
	struct node* temp
		= (struct node*)malloc(sizeof(struct node));
	temp->key = item;
	temp->left = NULL;
	temp->right = NULL;
	return temp;
}

```

TARGET EXECUTION PATH:
Path 1: START | START --> STATEMENT | struct node* temp
		= (struct node*)malloc(sizeof(struct node)); --> STATEMENT | temp->key = item; --> STATEMENT | temp->left = NULL; --> STATEMENT | temp->right = NULL; --> RETURN | return temp;

IMPORTANT: Choose inputs that satisfy this path's conditions.

